                <pb facs="0778" n="628" xml:id="pg628"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 3691/262.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Minister Lee to the Secretary of State.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Guatemala</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1907-03-29"><hi rendition="#italic">March 29,
                        1907</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Reports that Tegucigalpa was abandoned early yesterday and occupied last night by
                    forces of Nicaragua and revolutionists. Also reports that Chargé Brown advises
                    assumed charge with consuls to preserve order. Further reports that official
                    announcement has been received here that forces of Nicaragua were bombarding
                    Amapala to-day at noon and that general complication is to be feared.</p>
            </div>
